{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview","id":1116216,"title":"\u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 Preview!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-14T20:00:53-07:00","id":1116216,"title":"\u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 Preview!","content":"They are \u00d2r\u00ecshawesome <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kRVprZDluQkhrZ3c/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01...luQkhrZ3c/view</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T20:31:33-07:00","id":1116226,"title":"","content":"Every time I read one of these Previews I can feel all the work and energy they've put into researching these traditions, then assembling them into something fun to play.<br /> Also, I think that's a Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles reference in the Followers/Creatures. I hesitate to say it, but I don't think it can possibly be anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T22:26:42-07:00","id":1116253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116226#post1116226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I read one of these Previews I can feel all the work and energy they've put into researching these traditions, then assembling them into something fun to play.<br /> Also, I think that's a Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles reference in the Followers/Creatures. I hesitate to say it, but I don't think it can possibly be anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, I'm fairly sure<span style=\"color:#00000a\"> \u00d2</span>shun is Beyonc\u00e9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:25:12-07:00","id":1116263,"title":"","content":"I confess to knowing somewhere between Fuck and All about the Orisha, but I liked a lot of what I saw here. It's a pretty neat group of gathered divine beings. I especially liked Ogun, Oshun, Oya, and Moremi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:38:05-07:00","id":1116267,"title":"","content":"It will be interesting to see how these gods overlap with the Loa. Is Papa Legba a different God from Eshu Elegba, or a different cross-pantheons mantle? What about Kalfu, the Petwo counterpart to Rada Papa Legba, who captures the devil at the cross rods aspects of Eshu Elegba?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:49:15-07:00","id":1116273,"title":"","content":"The thing that I like about these Previews, is that not only do they showcase the wide variety of viewpoints that each path has, but do so in a way that is both enjoyable to understand, and fascinating to use in actual play. It can be all too easy to be overly academic or pompous when trying to provide new information, and I like how much better this does it than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 07-15-2017, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:54:02-07:00","id":1116277,"title":"","content":"Okay, might I ever so mutedly protest this line?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cFirst they came for the Titans, and I did not speak out \u2026.\u201d </div> </div> </div>For while I greatly appreciate the SJ-angle given to the Orisha, what with my whole German war-guilt-thing, I still think drawing parallels between our funny little Fantasy games and the real, actual Holocaust/Shoah is ... not good. Now the quote this line is drawn from is (luckily) from a German Lutheran pastor, not a Jewish person, but I still think the comparison is extremely inappropriate. Maybe it's different on the other side of the Atlantic, but where I come from, such allusions are touchy at best, and the source of nation-wide scandal at worst. The original author of that line, Pastor Martin Niem\u00f6ller, repeated it many times in the many speeches he gave as Holocaust survivor, swapping around all the people he had not spoken out for, the communists, the labour unions, the Catholics, the Jews, and obviously the touchiness differs between these categories, but in general, I don't find it entirely tasteful to equate any of the victims of the Holocaust/Shoah, the largest-scale genocide in history, with the likes of Apep and Fenrir, and comparing Zeus and Vishnu to Hitler, Himmler, and Goebbels. I can't tell anyone in Dev or otherwise what to do, but I can stress that I would sleep a lot tighter if lines like this one were avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T00:41:56-07:00","id":1116285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116277#post1116277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, might I ever so mutedly protest this line?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For while I greatly appreciate the SJ-angle given to the Orisha, what with my whole German war-guilt-thing, I still think drawing parallels between our funny little Fantasy games and the real, actual Holocaust/Shoah is ... not good. Now the quote this line is drawn from is (luckily) from a German Lutheran pastor, not a Jewish person, but I still think the comparison is extremely inappropriate. Maybe it's different on the other side of the Atlantic, but where I come from, such allusions are touchy at best, and the source of nation-wide scandal at worst. The original author of that line, Pastor Martin Niem\u00f6ller, repeated it many times in the many speeches he gave as Holocaust survivor, swapping around all the people he had not spoken out for, the communists, the labour unions, the Catholics, the Jews, and obviously the touchiness differs between these categories, but in general, I don't find it entirely tasteful to equate any of the victims of the Holocaust/Shoah, the largest-scale genocide in history, with the likes of Apep and Fenrir, and comparing Zeus and Vishnu to Hitler, Himmler, and Goebbels. I can't tell anyone in Dev or otherwise what to do, but I can stress that I would sleep a lot tighter if lines like this one were avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this very firmly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T00:48:00-07:00","id":1116287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116285#post1116285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconding this very firmly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh phew, I thought for a second it might have just been me and wasn't sure if I should mention it<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean, I could see the same sentiment of the &quot;What IS the big difference between a Titan and God? Are they really that different from us? Do they truly deserve our scorn?&quot; without pulling that reference out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-15-2017, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T03:39:53-07:00","id":1116315,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think Orisha would be clever enough not to break Godwin's Law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T04:19:31-07:00","id":1116324,"title":"","content":"I do like they finally discuss Olodumare, I brought up his absence in first ed and changed the whole pantheon to just ignore it. This version seems a step in the right direction. So are we going to get the Loa Orisha as a double spread pantheon? Or are they expanding into the loa later?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T04:28:41-07:00","id":1116326,"title":"","content":"Wait their weakness is oppression? What was the other pantheon's weakness, I don't remember. But I'm hesitant to have being a victim and being oppressed as universally defining to my character if I am one of the Orisha, I mean what about playing back on the continent, or better yet hundreds of years ago back on the continent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T04:54:49-07:00","id":1116331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116324#post1116324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like they finally discuss Olodumare, I brought up his absence in first ed and changed the whole pantheon to just ignore it. This version seems a step in the right direction. So are we going to get the Loa Orisha as a double spread pantheon? Or are they expanding into the loa later?</div> </div> </div> </div>Later, in the Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T05:24:33-07:00","id":1116333,"title":"","content":"I think the preview is great, for the most part.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do agree that the Godwin's Law issue seems a bit tone-deaf, and I agree with Eldagusto that &quot;oppression&quot; seems like a pretty poor weakness for the Orishas to have. But other than that, this is definitely a very interesting Pantheon and I like a lot of the stuff I'm seeing so far.<br /> <br /> This Pantheon can be called many things. &quot;Boring&quot; is definitely not one of them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:19:20-07:00","id":1116371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116326#post1116326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait their weakness is oppression? What was the other pantheon's weakness, I don't remember. But I'm hesitant to have being a victim and being oppressed as universally defining to my character if I am one of the Orisha, I mean what about playing back on the continent, or better yet hundreds of years ago back on the continent?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. A weakness should be something endemic to the pantheon itself, not something often suffered by its followers.<br /> <br /> Maybe &quot;lack of war footing&quot; could be pointed out as just as much a weakness as a strength when it comes to divine opposition-the Orisha have many virtues when it comes to universal acceptance, but sometimes a Titan (almost, if you ask them) deserves the moniker. They don't know how to act when the actual divine patron cannot be negotiated with-not because they don't think it can happen, but because they're adapted to human-scale threats. If Balor decided he wanted to make Nigeria his base for the counter-invasion of Ireland-well, they'd be inclined to let him have a small portion if their followers are willing to share their land and he helps them in return, he was there first. But if he doesn't think his parcel is large enough or cheats the deal, the Orishas would be a bit lost in how to keep him to his word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-15-2017, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T07:30:16-07:00","id":1116375,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who really doesn't know much about the Orisha (though who has picked up and is currently reading Mumbo Jumbo after having heard it mentioned multiple times on these forums and loving it so far) I really enjoyed reading that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll throw in my hat with the people who think the 'did not speak out' line is best removed, but that aside, this is a Preview that makes me want to play an Orisha Scion... and I can't give it better praise than that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The more I see of Mendez/Lula's work, the happier I am that he's the one in charge of the Deva as well... speaking of, as much as the two of them are on the opposite ends of the Titanomachy debate I find the Tradition/Innovation dichotomy to be eerily similar to the Duty/Conscience thing the Deva have going, in some ways, which I love and think could possibly be used by some of their Scions to find common ground.<br /> <br /> Also, A Wild Purview Appears! Is that one of the multiple new Purviews we were told about in the Shen update? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T09:53:53-07:00","id":1116448,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>: Good points about that quote. I'll cut it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>: Also very good points about the weakness. Neall and I are talking about some alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:54:43-07:00","id":1116471,"title":"","content":"I can see how oppression as a weakness would be difficult to work with depending on what you want to do with the World, but at the same time, oppression has such significant cultural implications to the Orisha and the way they're worshiped that I don't think cutting it out entirely would be a good idea either. <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I'd love to see a book that goes into religious and cultural conflicts like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T10:54:56-07:00","id":1116472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116448#post1116448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Good points about that quote. I'll cut it.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Also very good points about the weakness. Neall and I are talking about some alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for being receptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:04:26-07:00","id":1116476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116471#post1116471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, I'd love to see a book that goes into religious and cultural conflicts like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be kind of interesting, focus on how real world clashes of culture reflect with the gods and what it means. Not sure it could really be a whole book on its own but maybe a dedicated chapter in a later one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:33:31-07:00","id":1116488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116448#post1116448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>: Good points about that quote. I'll cut it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>: Also very good points about the weakness. Neall and I are talking about some alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the topic of the Orisha perception of other Pantheon's Titans Lula, a lot of what we see in the preview is mention of the... Sapient I guess is the right word? The Sapient Titans. Some Titans are not really 'Peope-y' and more colossal creatures. Hadi, Skoll, Apep, Jormungandr, Typhon, Namazu, those sorts of Titans. Ones who are just horrifically powerful animals more or less without any real stated capacity to communicate with others. How do the Orisha get along with them? It feels as though their, &quot;Titans are marginalized Pantheons,&quot; angle is workable in many cases, but it feels to be a bit unsteady in the face of the less human, the less conversation, and the purely wild. Of course, not all Titans who happen to be in the shape of animals are this way, Fenrir can speak and is cunning, Illuyanka is a giant snake but is probably a more reasonable authority figure than Tarhun, just some of the incredibly bestial Titans seem to not fit into their world view.<br /> <br /> My other question is how do they relate with the... I guess you could call them Flatly Antagonistic Titans. Izanami, for example, who sews death through the mortal world. Balor of the Evil Eye, a sea-faring, colonizing, conquering slaver. Isfet (Probably actually a Primordial to be fair) the opposite of Ma'at. Angra Mainyu, a great cosmic evil. (Also probably to be fair a Primordial) I can see how the Orisha might want bring peace with the more affable Titans, but the... 'Cosmic Evil,' figures, or you know, just Balor being an oppressive colonizing slaver. Are the Orisha still trying to 'make friends' there? Or do they sort of 'get' that some Titans are just not nice people. Not because they're Titans, just because they're personally cosmically antagonists, or just mean people.<br /> <br /> All well and good to make friends with Titans, I love the angle, gives the Orisha a rather unique outlook. But occasionally one of them's literally a personification of Evil. Not all the time, but, they crop up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-15-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:35:49-07:00","id":1116489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116375#post1116375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, A Wild Purview Appears! Is that one of the multiple new Purviews we were told about in the Shen update? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which purview? Frost? Beauty? Beauty got a mention in the Shen preview, IIRC, and Frost was mentioned way back in the Kickstarter as being in the Companion to be the sample Purview for &quot;And we're going to walk you through making your own Purview&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8310_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8310\" data-vbnamecard=\"8310\">Lula</a> - Thanks for listening. Once again you prove to be pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Water</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116488#post1116488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels as though their, &quot;Titans are marginalized Pantheons,&quot; angle is workable in many cases, but it feels to be a bit unsteady in the face of the less human, the less conversation, and the purely wild.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some friends of mine and I noted that it's a bit tough to try and maintain that ALL Titans are basically the victims of smear campaigns when Apep literally wants to eat the sun.<br /> <br /> Granted I can see the avenue for that being &quot;Okay yes well SOME of them are jerks... But frankly, LOKI'S a massive prick and you guys don't go around calling HIM a Titan.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-15-2017, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:45:23-07:00","id":1116492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116489#post1116489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which purview? Frost? Beauty? Beauty got a mention in the Shen preview, IIRC, and Frost was mentioned way back in the Kickstarter as being in the Companion to be the sample Purview for &quot;And we're going to walk you through making your own Purview&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Orunmila, Oshossi, Osanyin and Sonponna literally have a Wild Purview listed for them... that's what I was referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:46:38-07:00","id":1116493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116492#post1116492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Orunmila, Oshossi, Osanyin and Sonponna literally have a Wild Purview listed for them... that's what I was referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa shit I missed that ENTIRELY. Another thing to look forward to!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:15:58-07:00","id":1116502,"title":"","content":"I think Leliel has the right idea for a weakness.<br /> <br /> As I read the preview, I couldn't help but think &quot;Wow. If ANY of the Titans decide to take a swipe at these guys, they're going to be caught with their pants down!&quot; What's worse is that since they tend to be kinda preachy and dismissive toward the more pro-Titanomachy Pantheons, I could see a scenario in which those more war-ready Pantheons may be a little slow to respond if the Orishas got desperate enough to ask for their help. <br /> <br /> \u200bI could totally see Zeus saying something like &quot;The Orishas? Oh! You mean those guys who call us &quot;racists&quot; at every possible opportunity because we had the temerity to think that we should take the fight to these monsters that are now assailing them? Yeah, okay. We'll help. ARES! Assemble your armies..........but do be sure to tell them that there's no need to hurry. Let 'em sweat for a while.&quot; <br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah. Lack of war footing sounds like a much better weakness in my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:31:49-07:00","id":1116507,"title":"","content":"It's amazing writing and I'm pretty happy with it. The lines about the gods choosing to cross the Atlantic and shatter and reform are some good shivers. Clearly a lot of research put in.<br /> <br /> I'd echo concerns about the weakness. I think that &quot;structural oppression is our greatest weakness&quot; is probably a <i>true </i>statement but it rings differently in a writeup that doesn't really speak to any <i>other </i>weaknesses besides individual gods sometimes being kind of doofy. And it makes their take on the Titanomachy ring different too, though I imagine the rest of the book doesn't really say there is no reason but racism for fighting Titans.<br /> <br /> But y'all are already hearing that, looks like, which is why you remain the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 07-15-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T19:06:30-07:00","id":1116633,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have some mixed feelings on this one, to be honest. For the most part its pretty good and I can ignore the typos - I assume that it will get triple-checked before printing to add in the ocassional missing word - but ever now and then there's a sentence that I have some doubts about. The aforementioned Godwin's Law issue is one of them, but also sentences like '</span><i><span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In the Americas, the Night Doctors creep about under cover of darkness, abducting black folks American society forgets. They then experiment on their captives, transforming them into monsters, infecting them with syphilis to see what happens, or pumping them full of deadly experimental super-soldier serum.</span></span></i></span><span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">' also make me slightly nervous, for lack of a better term.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with real world stuff having a magical explanation in-game, but when you start getting into conspiracy theories I'm going to have some reservations, especially the &quot;The CIA invented aids and gave it to black people&quot; type of conspiracy theories, which is what I first thought of when I saw that. I don't have a problem with dealing with/addressing real world issues in game - its kind of necessary, especially for pantheons who are the patrons of people who face these issues like this one - but I feel like it should be handled a little bit more carefuly than this one did.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, I liked this one. Good work.</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T19:33:34-07:00","id":1116642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116633#post1116633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have some mixed feelings on this one, to be honest. For the most part its pretty good and I can ignore the typos - I assume that it will get triple-checked before printing to add in the ocassional missing word - but ever now and then there's a sentence that I have some doubts about. The aforementioned Godwin's Law issue is one of them, but also sentences like '</span><i><span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In the Americas, the Night Doctors creep about under cover of darkness, abducting black folks American society forgets. They then experiment on their captives, transforming them into monsters, infecting them with syphilis to see what happens, or pumping them full of deadly experimental super-soldier serum.</span></span></i></span><span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">' also make me slightly nervous, for lack of a better term.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with real world stuff having a magical explanation in-game, but when you start getting into conspiracy theories I'm going to have some reservations, especially the &quot;The CIA invented aids and gave it to black people&quot; type of conspiracy theories, which is what I first thought of when I saw that. I don't have a problem with dealing with/addressing real world issues in game - its kind of necessary, especially for pantheons who are the patrons of people who face these issues like this one - but I feel like it should be handled a little bit more carefuly than this one did.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, I liked this one. Good work.</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of thing has actually happened.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuskegee_syphilis_experiment\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuskeg...lis_experiment</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/tuskegee/timeline.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.cdc.gov/tuskegee/timeline.htm</a><br /> <br /> Yes. African Americans have had <i>real scientists</i> affiliated with a <i>government health organization</i> performing <i>highly unethical</i> research upon them. This group actually attempted to <i>deny treatment</i> to their subjects. This isn't a conspiracy theory; the <i>US Congress</i> instituted new laws to prevent it from ever happening again.<br /> <br /> They published this shit in <i>medical journals</i>. They felt <i>justified</i> in doing this.<br /> <br /> I wish this was just fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 07-15-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:15:20-07:00","id":1116666,"title":"","content":"The Tuskegee incident is just the most infamous. There are other crimes like through out US history","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:47:27-07:00","id":1116683,"title":"","content":"<b>Crying</b>, having put some thought into it I can see that you might have been aware of the United States' unethical medical history, and that you still felt that the aforementioned &quot;Night Doctors&quot; passage was an inappropriate derivation from real events combined with urban legends. I can see that viewpoint as being valid. RPGs have had some problems with dealing with delicate issues gracefully.<br /> <br /> However, I maintain that the Night Doctors and other such passages are the authors' way of getting across real tragedies in a way that can be explored through a myth-based RPG, and that author's choices more than likely came from a place of very real necessity. I believe this is not as great a misstep as you fear, though of course I defer to the actual line writers and developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T23:44:52-07:00","id":1116746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116448#post1116448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>: Good points about that quote. I'll cut it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a>: Also very good points about the weakness. Neall and I are talking about some alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for listening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And congrats on another great Preview, I didn't even mention that yesterday. Very New World focussed vs. me knowing mostly about the Old World Orisha, so very interesting to read on any account. Just thought that the entries were generally a bit shorter and simpler than in your Shen Preview. You think they'll be polished a bit more in another revision, or is that simply word count being reached? That's not even meant as criticism at this point, I've proclaimed loudly enough by now that I love how you present your pantheons - just wanna see a bit more of that, obviously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:27:26-07:00","id":1116754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116315#post1116315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think Orisha would be clever enough not to break Godwin's Law.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to be pedantic, but I'm going to be pedantic: Godwin's Law isn't a rule against referencing Nazism. Godwin's Law is the principle that as an online discussion continues, the liklihood of a Hitler/Nazism comparison approaches 1. It doesn't say anything about the aptness or appropriateness vs inappropriateness of the comparison. Obviously moot issue here as Lula agreed with criticism of tastefulness here, and is cutting the line, but still worth pointing out the actual meaning of Godwin's Law, since the inaccurate idea that it's a &quot;do not reference Nazism&quot; rule has been applied as a defense against actual core elements of fascism in modern politics being pointed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T12:12:13-07:00","id":1116937,"title":"","content":"So what does the Wild purview cover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:03:36-07:00","id":1116954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116754#post1116754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not to be pedantic, but I'm going to be pedantic: Godwin's Law isn't a rule against referencing Nazism. Godwin's Law is the principle that as an online discussion continues, the liklihood of a Hitler/Nazism comparison approaches 1. It doesn't say anything about the aptness or appropriateness vs inappropriateness of the comparison. Obviously moot issue here as Lula agreed with criticism of tastefulness here, and is cutting the line, but still worth pointing out the actual meaning of Godwin's Law, since the inaccurate idea that it's a &quot;do not reference Nazism&quot; rule has been applied as a defense against actual core elements of fascism in modern politics being pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also false is the &quot;you automatically lose if you invoke Nazis.&quot; Or &quot;the discussion is over if you invoke Nazis.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T01:33:43-07:00","id":1117125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116754#post1116754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not to be pedantic, but I'm going to be pedantic: Godwin's Law isn't a rule against referencing Nazism. Godwin's Law is the principle that as an online discussion continues, the liklihood of a Hitler/Nazism comparison approaches 1. It doesn't say anything about the aptness or appropriateness vs inappropriateness of the comparison. Obviously moot issue here as Lula agreed with criticism of tastefulness here, and is cutting the line, but still worth pointing out the actual meaning of Godwin's Law, since the inaccurate idea that it's a &quot;do not reference Nazism&quot; rule has been applied as a defense against actual core elements of fascism in modern politics being pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. It's just that in recent years the definition of Godwin's Law has seemingly expanded, for better or for worse, to also include use of Reductio ad Hilterum, which is basically just an ad hominem attack that involves calling someone a Nazi for no good reason. So I figured calling them out for breaking it in this instance on account of the quote was appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 07-17-2017, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:07:42-07:00","id":1117168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117125#post1117125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. It's just that in recent years the definition of Godwin's Law has seemingly expanded, for better or for worse, to also include use of Reductio ad Hilterum, which is basically just an ad hominem attack that involves calling someone a Nazi for no good reason. So I figured calling them out for breaking it in this instance on account of the quote was appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the subclauses mentioned by resplendent fire exist. While referencing Nazi's can sometimes be a valid point, it more often means that the user has run out of genuinely compelling points and has to resort to linking the other view to Nazi's.<br /> <br /> Extreme strawman example. Hitler was a vegan, therefore vegans are evil bigoted facists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:01:26-07:00","id":1117225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1116937#post1116937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what does the Wild purview cover?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Wild</b><br /> This is the Purview of untamed lands and the flora of the wilderness, wielded by Gods of nature or plants. It rules all wilderness, from forests and jungles to desert cacti to taiga evergreens. Its miracles can animate or control plant life, preserve the wilderness against human settlement, or draw on symbolic associations of wildness to unleash the inner beast of domesticated animals or humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:21:52-07:00","id":1117241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117225#post1117225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wild</b><br /> This is the Purview of untamed lands and the flora of the wilderness, wielded by Gods of nature or plants. It rules all wilderness, from forests and jungles to desert cacti to taiga evergreens. Its miracles can animate or control plant life, preserve the wilderness against human settlement, or draw on symbolic associations of wildness to unleash the inner beast of domesticated animals or humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sonds Awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:15:35-07:00","id":1117267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117225#post1117225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wild</b><br /> This is the Purview of untamed lands and the flora of the wilderness, wielded by Gods of nature or plants. It rules all wilderness, from forests and jungles to desert cacti to taiga evergreens. Its miracles can animate or control plant life, preserve the wilderness against human settlement, or draw on symbolic associations of wildness to unleash the inner beast of domesticated animals or humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>So sort of a blend of Beast and Fertility with a focus on more wild and feral usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:12:10-07:00","id":1117292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117267#post1117267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So sort of a blend of Beast and Fertility with a focus on more wild and feral usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fertility covers lands tamed by human effort and domesticated plants; Wild covers that which humanity has yet to master. One of the reasons it was created is because there were many Gods, like Osh\u00f3ss\u00ed, with ties to the wilderness and whose Scions would appreciate plant-based powers, but who aren't actually fertility gods. <br /> <br /> It doesn't directly overlap with Beasts - it can strip away the edifice of civilization from domesticated animals, but it can do the same to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:17:41-07:00","id":1117300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117225#post1117225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wild</b><br /> This is the Purview of untamed lands and the flora of the wilderness, wielded by Gods of nature or plants. It rules all wilderness, from forests and jungles to desert cacti to taiga evergreens. Its miracles can animate or control plant life, preserve the wilderness against human settlement, or draw on symbolic associations of wildness to unleash the inner beast of domesticated animals or humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that's awesome! Each and every teased tidbit just makes me MORE excited!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:25:37-07:00","id":1117305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117292#post1117292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fertility covers lands tamed by human effort and domesticated plants; Wild covers that which humanity has yet to master. One of the reasons it was created is because there were many Gods, like Osh\u00f3ss\u00ed, with ties to the wilderness and whose Scions would appreciate plant-based powers, but who aren't actually fertility gods.<br /> <br /> It doesn't directly overlap with Beasts - it can strip away the edifice of civilization from domesticated animals, but it can do the same to humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, would it also be applicable for Gods like Shiva and Kali who have connections to and in some aspects represent the breakdown of civilization and social conventions, but aren't directly associated with plant life? Or is that better represented by Chaos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:05:50-07:00","id":1117391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117305#post1117305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder, would it also be applicable for Gods like Shiva and Kali who have connections to and in some aspects represent the breakdown of civilization and social conventions, but aren't directly associated with plant life? Or is that better represented by Chaos?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Chaos's bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:16:11-07:00","id":1117433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117168#post1117168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why the subclauses mentioned by resplendent fire exist. While referencing Nazi's can sometimes be a valid point, it more often means that the user has run out of genuinely compelling points and has to resort to linking the other view to Nazi's.<br /> <br /> Extreme strawman example. Hitler was a vegan, therefore vegans are evil bigoted facists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. Even though I said those two clauses are false, I meant that they aren't true <i>every single time it happens</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:26:02-07:00","id":1117495,"title":"","content":"To make a more positive contribution to the thread, I'd like to say I find the image of Oya Iyansan laughing like the predator whilst soaring up into a tornado to be immensely evocative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:48:54-07:00","id":1117550,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed this preview. I sympathise with the Orishas' position on the Titanomachy, and I like that there's a pantheon that's standing up for the Titans who aren't complete monsters. I'm sure that they're smart enough that they wouldn't let the truly malevolent Titans lay waste to them if it came to that. They certainly have members who could hold their own against them if they had to. I personally like the god/titan divide to be more political than not, and I'm a strong supporter of the idea of having playable scions of Titans.<br /> <br /> Oya remains my personal favorite member of the pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:51:20-07:00","id":1117552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117495#post1117495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make a more positive contribution to the thread, I'd like to say I find the image of Oya Iyansan laughing like the predator whilst soaring up into a tornado to be immensely evocative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally my favorite bit was that Orisha-oko and Baldur are considered adorable when they hang out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:40:34-07:00","id":1117572,"title":"","content":"Can I say, I am proud of this forum?<br /> <br /> Four pages, and the biggest complaint is &quot;Um, guys, isn't the weakness a bit Mary Sue-ish?&quot; Not a single whine from actual racists complaining it exists in the first place or downplaying oppression as a problem.<br /> <br /> I love you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T01:47:15-07:00","id":1117640,"title":"","content":"Are the Kami also anti-Titanomachy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T02:23:35-07:00","id":1117647,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty sizable number of evil gods/demons/giant monsters in Japanese mythology that are fairly malevolent and destructive, so I think the Kami would have more reason than the Orisha to be in conflict with certain Titans at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T03:29:41-07:00","id":1117660,"title":"","content":"Given this bit from the Shen preview I think it's safe to say they are not exactly Titan friendly:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Shen have important, formalized working relationships with the Devas and Kami. The South and East Asian pantheons share a non-discriminating attitude towards the simultaneous practice of multiple religions, as well as an aggressive stance towards titans (though there\u2019s some disagreement as to what to do with the titans after you knock them out).&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't mind some more Kami previews... I feel like of all the Pantheons in the core, we know the least about them, though that may totally just be me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T04:07:53-07:00","id":1117666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117660#post1117660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given this bit from the Shen preview I think it's safe to say they are not exactly Titan friendly:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Shen have important, formalized working relationships with the Devas and Kami. The South and East Asian pantheons share a non-discriminating attitude towards the simultaneous practice of multiple religions, as well as an aggressive stance towards titans (though there\u2019s some disagreement as to what to do with the titans after you knock them out).&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't mind some more Kami previews... I feel like of all the Pantheons in the core, we know the least about them, though that may totally just be me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Manitou are the least well-known now that we have this nice, juicy preview for the Orishas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T04:24:55-07:00","id":1117669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117666#post1117666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say the Manitou are the least well-known now that we have this nice, juicy preview for the Orishas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the Manitou we know their Virtues of Pride and Purpose, we had an amazing write-up by the author on his experiences writing them, we have a Preview of their PSP boons, and we know their general outlook on the Titanomachy from the post Lula did some time back (which didn't mention the Kami at all). For the Kami, we know their Virtues (but then we know all ten Virtue Sets) and we know the name of their PSP... that's kind of it, unless I missed something... I mean, I would totally love either of these Pantheons previewed (and if I was being honest I would obviously want the Deva previewed next) but I feel the Kami overall have been in the spotlight the least.<br /> <br /> Edit : Oh, wait, did you mean that in the sense of general public knowledge? Then yes, definitely the Manitou... sorry, I should have been clearer, I meant in terms of preview material for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-18-2017, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T05:05:09-07:00","id":1117676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117669#post1117669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for the Manitou we know their Virtues of Pride and Purpose, we had an amazing write-up by the author on his experiences writing them, we have a Preview of their PSP boons, and we know their general outlook on the Titanomachy from the post Lula did some time back (which didn't mention the Kami at all). For the Kami, we know their Virtues (but then we know all ten Virtue Sets) and we know the name of their PSP... that's kind of it, unless I missed something... I mean, I would totally love either of these Pantheons previewed (and if I was being honest I would obviously want the Deva previewed next) but I feel the Kami overall have been in the spotlight the least.<br /> <br /> Edit : Oh, wait, did you mean that in the sense of general public knowledge? Then yes, definitely the Manitou... sorry, I should have been clearer, I meant in terms of preview material for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually, I guess we're both right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm right as far as general knowledge goes, and you're right as far as &quot;How much do we know about this Pantheon in the game thus far.&quot; So, yeah, some solid Kami information would definitely be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T06:40:34-07:00","id":1117702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117647#post1117647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a pretty sizable number of evil gods/demons/giant monsters in Japanese mythology that are fairly malevolent and destructive, so I think the Kami would have more reason than the Orisha to be in conflict with certain Titans at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An evil god isn't necessarily a Titan. As far as we've seen, Titans are defined from gods by being more dominated by their purview, and less fatebound to humanity, making them more primal expressions of their dominating purview rather than playing out more human dramas writ-cosmic ala gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:43:21-07:00","id":1117727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117572#post1117572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I say, I am proud of this forum?<br /> <br /> Four pages, and the biggest complaint is &amp;quot;Um, guys, isn't the weakness a bit Mary Sue-ish?&amp;quot; Not a single whine from actual racists complaining it exists in the first place or downplaying oppression as a problem.<br /> <br /> I love you guys.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay I'll be the bad guy, although not racist, and say I didn't care for it, its delibrately baiting people with a pile of PC jargon.<br /> <br /> Slavery is evil, no shit right, but slavery in Africa existed long before white people and the horrors of colonialism, its was Africans who sold people to the Slave traders, and the Orisha seem to have no complaints about that.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out there were many white people who opposed slavery, and hundreds of thousands of Yankees who died to end the practice in America (it was already illegal in Canada, and the rest of the British Empire, while Africans were still owning slaves).<br /> <br /> That of course doesn't excuse the monstereous white merchants who engaged in the Slave trade, but I merely point out that its more complex then white people bad, black people good. Ghana in fact gave an official apology to the African American.<br /> <br /> Also when pointing to locations, you left out Canada, which has a quickly growing Haitian population, especially in Montreal, speaking French is a huge asset.<br /> <br /> I know I'll be falsely accused of racism, which is annoying, but this &quot;priveldge&quot; nonesense does breeds racial division.<br /> <br /> And no I don't deny racism against black people still exists, I've gotten into massive arguements with people over it, I just believe its possible to reject PC extremism, while supporting the humanity and dignity of all humans races. <br /> <br /> Look I just think its possible to take a balanced approach, you don't have to ignore the historically wrongs commited against African Americans, but also without cherry picking historically facts to push a Intersectionalist narrative.<br /> <br /> Example I support BLM when it does smart things like pushing for manaditory body cams for police, and I oppose it when it sabotages Toronto's Gay Pride Parade. Balance approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:17:02-07:00","id":1117744,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to appreciate a fictional rendition of a pantheon, designed for a role-playing game, set in an alternate world, without constantly dragging the discussion into arguments and debates on real-world nazism or racism? In a minute, it's going to be impossible to present <i>anything </i>without stepping on someone's toes. I thought the Gods as presented were playable, entertaining, and a decent representation of the Orisha. I'm now concerned that when the Manitou are previewed (or just included in the game when it comes out), there will be a huge chorus of complaints over how they are presented that will drown out any fun to be had with the game itself. I don't want an historically accurate, painstakingly-detailed breakdown of every pantheon and culture included, that is sanitized to the point that no-one can ever be offended/concerned, because you can never please everyone. I just want a considerate, well-written, and fun game about the chosen of the Gods on an alternate Earth, and some compromise is inevitable, or this is never getting past production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:22:15-07:00","id":1117748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117727#post1117727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slavery is evil, no shit right, but slavery in Africa existed long before white people and the horrors of colonialism, its was Africans who sold people to the Slave traders, and the Orisha seem to have no complaints about that.<br /> <br /> I'll also point out there were many white people who opposed slavery, and hundreds of thousands of Yankees who died to end the practice in America (it was already illegal in Canada, and the rest of the British Empire, while Africans were still owning slaves).<br /> <br /> That of course doesn't excuse the monstereous white merchants who engaged in the Slave trade, but I merely point out that its more complex then white people bad, black people good. Ghana in fact gave an official apology to the African American.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just to make a comment on this as a historian. Slavery is a really ineffective word, the degrees of variation within systems of slavery are vast, and by simply using the single word 'Slavery' to refer to everything from the Chattel Slavery of the Triangle Trade, to Roman Debt Slavery, to Irish Slave-Raiding, Haida Slavery, Ashanti Slavery, or Yoruban Slavery causes a massive degree of confusion. It's like the word 'God' or 'King,' they just confuse everything since a Theoi is not a Deva is not a Shen and yet are all Gods, theoretically. Same with a Ri, a Rex, a King, and an Inca.<br /> <br /> So, the Orisha (and actually probably almost every Pantheon that cares what mortals get up to) would entirely legitimately be horrified and opposed to the Chattel Slavery they see with the Triangle Trade. While, yes, the Yoruban people had a slave system, (though I will admit I know more about the Ashanti system) it was entirely different from Chattel Slavery of the Triangle Trade. This system developed to be a focus on the construct of 'race,' degrading a population to be sub-human, and it worked people to death in a massive number. This was entirely different from the traditional system the Orisha would be used to.<br /> <br /> In my games, I normally rule that all of the slave-taking Pantheons range between confused, to disgusted with the practice of the Triangle Trade. The Theoi, Tuatha, Aesir, Abosom, Orisha, etc all had slave systems, but the system that developed with the Triangle Trade was exceptionally different than these other systems (which were also all different from each other) and doesn't make sense from their perspectives. Some think it's just another example of mortals being stupid (Theoi, Tuatha) while others are grossly opposed to it (Orisha, Abosom).<br /> <br /> So, while, yes, Slavery was present in Africa before the development of the Triangle Trade, that likely doesn't mean much to the Orisha, or other Pantheons. They know what slavery 'ought' to be, the cultural systems for it, laws, religious functions of slaves, method to taking slaves, method to freeing slaves, etc. (which they mostly all disagree with each other over) They know that the Triangle Trade system violates their traditional system, devastated their worshiper base, and was in gross disrespect of life itself. Shango would have had slaves once, I don't know if he would any more, but his slaves would be bound by an entire different set of cultural values, laws, and systems to what the Orisha experience with the Triangle Trade. I can entirely see the entire Triangle Trade having essentially caused a 'cultural scar' on the Orisha, causing a total dropping of their traditional system to stand stalwart against slave systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-18-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:25:52-07:00","id":1117753,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> : For your perusal I suggest skipping to 7:25 on this video: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jk3iOqKOD7g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jk3iOqKOD7g<br /> <br /> E</a>dit : though I see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> has already covered it while I was just typing this out with his signature academic flair <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-18-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:29:45-07:00","id":1117758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117727#post1117727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay I'll be the bad guy, although not racist, and say I didn't care for it, its delibrately baiting people with a pile of PC jargon.<br /> <br /> Slavery is evil, no shit right, but slavery in Africa existed long before white people and the horrors of colonialism, its was Africans who sold people to the Slave traders, and the Orisha seem to have no complaints about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The debt slavery that existed before the chattel market of Transatlantic trade was introduced is not REMOTELY comparable to what existed after. There's a reason in those later years of African slavery you're referencing, Dahomey was a Brazilian puppet regime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:12:40-07:00","id":1117789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117727#post1117727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'll be the bad guy, although not racist, and say I didn't care for it, its delibrately baiting people with a pile of PC jargon.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Claiming that the author is deliberately baiting people is a personal attack. Furthermore, the rest of your post is a significant departure from the topic at hand, which seemingly serves only to spark discussion of controversial political topics. This is a clear rule 2 violation. This also appears to be part of a consistent pattern with your posting behavior, seizing any opportunity to drive discussion in the direction of your personal politics. I'm issuing a one week suspension, and if this habit continues, you will face longer-term loss of posting privileges.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:35:39-07:00","id":1117805,"title":"","content":"Great preview! I've enjoyed the tone as much as the information, and that's saying something. I have, however, one (maybe dumb) question: Are Papa Ghede/Baron Samedi being considered as part of Papa Legba, or have they dissappeared? I'd miss them dearly if that'd be the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T09:50:55-07:00","id":1117812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117805#post1117805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great preview! I've enjoyed the tone as much as the information, and that's saying something. I have, however, one (maybe dumb) question: Are Papa Ghede/Baron Samedi being considered as part of Papa Legba, or have they dissappeared? I'd miss them dearly if that'd be the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There has been talk of having the Loa as their own Pantheon, or, sub-Pantheon, or similar sort of idea. Baron Samedi will likely be in there, and I can't wait to see him! I have got a thing for Skeletons that the Tuatha just can't provide.<br /> <br /> Papa Legba, I believe, is Eshu. He was broken into two Deities IIRC, Legba and Kalfu, as the religious traditions shifted. Lula who actually knows about the details of this could probably tell some more delicious details about the split though since they actually know about the topic compared to myself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:04:58-07:00","id":1117897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1117812#post1117812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There has been talk of having the Loa as their own Pantheon, or, sub-Pantheon, or similar sort of idea. Baron Samedi will likely be in there, and I can't wait to see him! I have got a thing for Skeletons that the Tuatha just can't provide.<br /> <br /> Papa Legba, I believe, is Eshu. He was broken into two Deities IIRC, Legba and Kalfu, as the religious traditions shifted. Lula who actually knows about the details of this could probably tell some more delicious details about the split though since they actually know about the topic compared to myself!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh wait, you are absolutely right Watcher, i completely forgot about the very first kickstarter achievement. Facepalm. Thank you for reminding me! Anyway, i second you: i'd welcome any more detail about Legba!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T18:43:06-07:00","id":1118022,"title":"","content":"Neat seeing a pantheon that I don't know much about detailed. I feel bad that I find myself defaulting to the French aliases because the native language is unfamiliar to me. Could I get links to other pantheon previews, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T21:08:38-07:00","id":1118057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1118022#post1118022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat seeing a pantheon that I don't know much about detailed. I feel bad that I find myself defaulting to the French aliases because the native language is unfamiliar to me. Could I get links to other pantheon previews, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I know my ignorant ass will default to the Roman names for the Netjer (Ra, Anubis, Set, Horus) because those are the sames I've known them by for decades. Please don't be mad, Lex.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for some other Previews...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kM2trLVMwNGJXM2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Chinese Shen</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kcEYwbnRrMjBHY1k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Some Paths and Purviews, both General and Pantheon-Specific</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kU2E5OXlhZm56Vjg%20%20\" target=\"_blank\">Fate-related Paths and Purviews, including Fate, Fortune, and Prosperity</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd3h1aFp1b1J3ODg/view\" target=\"_blank\">Some previews for various Terra Incognita</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sZhxhPlepq3wEawVoFNIrIaYzwtG-0_h5bUl9ujS_DY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Aztec Teotl Pantheon</a><br /> <br /> There was a preview for the Nejter, but it was lukewarmly received and it's being edited and will be previewed in the next update, I believe...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kZDNGdDBWaVJZX2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Irish Tuatha de Dannan</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kZmtQNHJjd3cyRkE\" target=\"_blank\">And the Greek/Roman Theoi</a><br /> <br /> I THINK that's the downloadable previews we've had... There's been a few smaller ones in the Kickstarter itself, like previews for Relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T16:39:45-07:00","id":1119673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1118057#post1118057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I know my ignorant ass will default to the Roman names for the Netjer (Ra, Anubis, Set, Horus) because those are the sames I've known them by for decades. Please don't be mad, Lex.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for some other Previews...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kM2trLVMwNGJXM2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Chinese Shen</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kcEYwbnRrMjBHY1k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Some Paths and Purviews, both General and Pantheon-Specific</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kU2E5OXlhZm56Vjg%20%20\" target=\"_blank\">Fate-related Paths and Purviews, including Fate, Fortune, and Prosperity</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd3h1aFp1b1J3ODg/view\" target=\"_blank\">Some previews for various Terra Incognita</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sZhxhPlepq3wEawVoFNIrIaYzwtG-0_h5bUl9ujS_DY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Aztec Teotl Pantheon</a><br /> <br /> There was a preview for the Nejter, but it was lukewarmly received and it's being edited and will be previewed in the next update, I believe...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kZDNGdDBWaVJZX2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Irish Tuatha de Dannan</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kZmtQNHJjd3cyRkE\" target=\"_blank\">And the Greek/Roman Theoi</a><br /> <br /> I THINK that's the downloadable previews we've had... There's been a few smaller ones in the Kickstarter itself, like previews for Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, thank you kindly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T01:55:38-07:00","id":1119805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1118057#post1118057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I know my ignorant ass will default to the Roman names for the Netjer (Ra, Anubis, Set, Horus) because those are the sames I've known them by for decades. Please don't be mad, Lex.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for some other Previews...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kM2trLVMwNGJXM2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Chinese Shen</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kcEYwbnRrMjBHY1k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Some Paths and Purviews, both General and Pantheon-Specific</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kU2E5OXlhZm56Vjg%20%20\" target=\"_blank\">Fate-related Paths and Purviews, including Fate, Fortune, and Prosperity</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kd3h1aFp1b1J3ODg/view\" target=\"_blank\">Some previews for various Terra Incognita</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sZhxhPlepq3wEawVoFNIrIaYzwtG-0_h5bUl9ujS_DY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Aztec Teotl Pantheon</a><br /> <br /> There was a preview for the Nejter, but it was lukewarmly received and it's being edited and will be previewed in the next update, I believe...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kZDNGdDBWaVJZX2M/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Irish Tuatha de Dannan</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B01LwCGSbE8kZmtQNHJjd3cyRkE\" target=\"_blank\">And the Greek/Roman Theoi</a><br /> <br /> I THINK that's the downloadable previews we've had... There's been a few smaller ones in the Kickstarter itself, like previews for Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't mis-name the Pantheon that places the most import on true names! You fool!<br /> <br /> Djehuti is going to be very displeased with you. Also, you're passing up the chance to say &quot;Djehuti.&quot; Come on and try that one out loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T06:57:58-07:00","id":1119867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1119805#post1119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't mis-name the Pantheon that places the most import on true names! You fool!<br /> <br /> Djehuti is going to be very displeased with you. Also, you're passing up the chance to say &quot;Djehuti.&quot; Come on and try that one out loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, But if true names give you power over them wouldn't they want you to use the wrong names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:03:57-07:00","id":1119955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1119805#post1119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't mis-name the Pantheon that places the most import on true names! You fool!<br /> <br /> Djehuti is going to be very displeased with you. Also, you're passing up the chance to say &quot;Djehuti.&quot; Come on and try that one out loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's an unpopular opinion on these forums, but no one can reconstruct the names of the Egyptian deities accurately (incidentally, my Egyptology prof explained that today again). Djehuti is just as inaccurate as Thoth, because hieroglyphic writing doesn't record most vowels, and thus to fill them in is anyone's guess. In that regard, everyone is a fool, I guess. It's information that's just lost, and at least we know how to pronounce Thoth, unlike \u1e0f\u1e25wty. So I really don't get why people crusade about that so hard ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:08:01-07:00","id":1119959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1119955#post1119955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it's an unpopular opinion on these forums, but no one can reconstruct the names of the Egyptian deities accurately (incidentally, my Egyptology prof explained that today again). Djehuti is just as inaccurate as Thoth, because hieroglyphic writing doesn't record most vowels, and thus to fill them in is anyone's guess. In that regard, everyone is a fool, I guess. It's information that's just lost, and at least we know how to pronounce Thoth, unlike \u1e0f\u1e25wty. So I really don't get why people crusade about that so hard ...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;We can never truly get the Egyptian names right, so let's not bother trying and just use the ones of their Greek conquerors instead&quot; seems more than a little foolish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:13:47-07:00","id":1119960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1116216-\u00f2r\u00ecsh\u00e0-preview?p=1119805#post1119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't mis-name the Pantheon that places the most import on true names! You fool!<br /> <br /> Djehuti is going to be very displeased with you. Also, you're passing up the chance to say &quot;Djehuti.&quot; Come on and try that one out loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's too late for me! It's like trying to get me to call it 'pop'! It just doesn't stick!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T16:23:49-07:00","id":1122120,"title":"","content":"Really enjoyed this read! Lots of good stuff in there. Though I'm confused as to why they decided to lump Olokun and Yemoja together. They are totally different beings who do totally different beings. I'm not saying Olokun has to be added, (even though I think Olokun could qualify as a Titan just like Sharpona) I just don't think Olokun should be used as a secondary name for Yemoja. I'm also pleasantly surprised to see Ijapa! He was the companion of my old Obatala scion, and I'm glad to see I'm not the only one who thinks he's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11009-starman","name":"StarMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T17:03:43-08:00","id":1179980,"title":"","content":"I know I'm very late on this, but I want to agree with Starman that different individuals shouldn't be made into one, and Olokun definitely fits as a titan. <br /> <br /> I also think Obatal\u00e1 got a short stick here. This isn't really reflected in the purviews, but the write-up for him is just about how a king said he tricked Obatal\u00e1 one time - even though Oduduwa's description does convey the notion that he might just be full of it. But Obatal\u00e1 is known for having the greatest ach\u00e9, which goes together for being the eldest, and for possessing the wisdom of both genders. He is the wisest, which is why he's the leader, and he's also the one in charge of diplomacy and peace, which for some reason wound up on Orisha Oko's description instead. I don't know if Yoruba in Africa no longer place importance on Obatal\u00e1, but at least in Cuban Lucum\u00ed he is arguably the most highly revered of the Orisha, and one of the five that every aborisha receives along with Osh\u00fan, Ellegu\u00e1, Yemay\u00e1, and Shang\u00f3.<br /> <br /> I also think that the emphasis on tolerance paints with a bit too broad a brush, to the extent that it gets perspectives on gender into the mix that aren't actually supposed to be there. Mostly related to complete disregard of the fact that it's an initiatory religion. This also comes up when it says (in Orunmila's description) that anyone can throw nuts or cowries - no, an aleyo definitely can't, and depending on lineage maybe an aborisha can't either, some say it's only to olorisha. But apparently Orunmila initiates women now? There is nothing intolerant about the orisha as a whole, but an individual orisha only crowns someone very similar to himself, which is why orunmila only crowns heterosexual men. An orisha who is gendered only crowns those of their own gender. Some others like Obatal\u00e1 (who normally uses male pronouns by default, despite not being gendered) or Olokun (normally female pronouns) or Ibeji (who, unlike Obatal\u00e1, does use singular they) can take both genders, and Ellegu\u00e1 does too just because he's about communicating with difference. But gendered Orisha don't normally commune directly across lines, and Orunmila especially doesn't, he doesn't even commune with the faith in general very closely, If\u00e1 is sort of a separate thing that just is compatible and shares cultural heritage.<br /> <br /> I also felt like there was a flaw of the numbers - Ibeji is both two and one, which was dealt with okay. They detail of their scions was odd but I don't know if there's a better way of doing it. But Olodumare is three and one, which wasn't referenced at all except by listing all three facets as if they were just different names. I know that there's an aversion to monotheism in general, and Trinity is a Christian thing, but that doesn't change that it's also a part of the regla de Osh\u00e1.<br /> <br /> I also thought it strange that ex\u00fa was used as a name for Ellegu\u00e1 rather than a title, but the write-up went to such pains to use &quot;camino&quot; instead of the yoruba version but didn't do that for any other word. But it seems that he is sometimes referred to this way by some Brazilians. Although on the subject of Brazilians, it seems odd that there was all that talk of Candombl\u00e9 but none of Umbanda, even though I know Quimbanda would have conflicted with the idea that this portrayal of the Orisha (like most) doesn't truck with human sacrifice, and they're apparently very different in how they worship anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12463-cruxador","name":"Cruxador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12463_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}